{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Like an arrow</b> — He likens the touch of El to an arrow, and the meaning: until an arrow pierces his liver, and he will not accept reproof." "<b>Like a bird hastening</b> — So quickly will an arrow pierce him, and the fool does not know that on account of his soul dying he hates reproof, and this is the correct interpretation."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:21.375848982Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}